  "summary": "Review Week 12 in one story: a class presentation about a greener city, with إِذَا sentences, passive verbs, a formal letter and a polite debate.",
  "intro": "Today is review day, مُرَاجَعَة. Sami's group gives a تَقْدِيم (presentation) about a greener city, and every part of the week comes back. The problem and the solution use إِذَا + a past verb: إِذَا اسْتَعْمَلْنَا الْحَافِلَةَ، قَلَّ التَّلَوُّثُ (if we use the bus, pollution goes down). The facts use the passive, made by changing the vowels: بُنِيَتْ (it was built), تُوَلَّدُ (it is generated), يُسْتَعْمَلُ (it is used). The formal letter opens with تَحِيَّةً طَيِّبَةً وَبَعْدُ, the debate needs لَا أُوَافِقُ (I don't agree) and a reason, and the talk is held together by أَوَّلًا، ثُمَّ and أَخِيرًا. A presentation ends with شُكْرًا لِحُسْنِ الِاسْتِمَاع (thank you for listening).",
  "objectives": [
    "Give a short presentation in Arabic, organised with أَوَّلًا، ثُمَّ and أَخِيرًا",
    "Use إِذَا + a past verb to say what happens if we change something",
    "Recognise and use passive verbs like بُنِيَتْ (it was built) and يُسْتَعْمَلُ (it is used)",
    "Open a formal letter and agree or disagree in a debate with a reason"
